      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of days from November 23 to December 23.\n2. Determine how many days this interval spans in terms of the week.\n\nFirst, calculate the number of days from November 23 to December 23:\n- There are 30 days in November.\n- From November 23 to December 1 is 23 days.\n- From December 2 to December 23 is 21 days.\nSo, the total number of days from November 23 to December 23 is:\n\\[ 23 + 21 = 44 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many complete weeks and extra days are in 44 days. Since there are 7 days in a week, we divide 44 by 7:\n\\[ 44 \\div 7 = 6 \\text{ weeks and } 2 \\text{ days} \\]\nThis means that 44 days is equivalent to 6 full weeks and 2 extra days. Starting from a Thursday, moving forward 6 weeks brings us to a Tuesday (because starting from Thursday, moving 6 days forward gives Tuesday). Then adding the 2 extra days from the 44th day:\n\\[ Tuesday + 2 \\text{ days} = Thursday \\]\n\nTherefore, December 23 is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Tuesday}}\\).",
